        "subject": "LU-20790 efalnd: Release and refill failed Rx buffers",
        "message": "LU-20790 efalnd: Release and refill failed Rx buffers\n\nOn the initial Rx handling error paths the buffer is freed but the RQ is\nnot refilled, which depletes the RQ over time. Refill the RQ on the\nerror path as well.\n\nIn addition, a zero length completion returned without releasing the\nbuffer at all, leaking it together with its RQ slot. Route that case\nthrough the error path too. Since byte_len is only meaningful for a\nsuccessful completion, clear the posted marker as soon as the buffer is\nours and set the received length only after the completion is known to\nbe good, as both kefalnd_free_rx() and kefalnd_refill_rx() require a\nnon-negative rx_nob.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nFixes: 0c773016d837 (\"LU-18977 efalnd: Introduce AWS EFA Lustre network driver\")\nSigned-off-by: Yonatan Nachum <ynachum@amazon.com>\nSigned-off-by: Zanhua Huang <zanhua@amazon.com>\nChange-Id: I757ee5a243396c7fc3483600641991f7dbac56d4\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/69314\nReviewed-by: Timothy Day <timday@thelustrecollective.com>\nReviewed-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\n"
      },
